OL,3,GNEWSAAfter 323 days adventurer nears
OL,4,Aend of epic oceans row
OL,5,
OL,6,FA former Royal Marine looks set to
OL,7,Fcomplete a record-breaking challenge,
OL,8,Fhaving rowed solo and unsupported
OL,9,Facross the Pacific and Indian Ocean.
OL,11,FDave 'Dinger' Bell, from Bere Regis,
OL,12,FDorset, set off from the west coast of
OL,13,FPeru on 9 November last year and has
OL,14,Fnot stopped or set foot on land for 323
OL,15,Fdays.
OL,17,FDuring the journey, he has been
OL,18,Ffollowed by "man-eating" sharks,
OL,19,Fcrossed snake and crocodile-infested
OL,20,Fwaters and lost two oars in a storm
OL,21,Fwhich also damaged his boat.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
